8. Design Philosophy

MOS is founded upon five philosophical assumptions.

8.1 Cognition over Conversation

Conversations are observations.

Knowledge is cognition.

MOS stores cognition rather than chat history.

8.2 Evidence before Truth

Truth is rarely absolute.

Knowledge emerges from evidence.
Beliefs evolve as evidence changes.

8.3 Explainability by Design

Every cognitive artifact SHALL be explainable.

The system SHALL always be capable of describing why it reached a conclusion.

8.4 Continuous Evolution

Memory is never static.

Reflection, learning, and evidence continuously reshape knowledge.

8.5 Separation of Concerns

Observation, memory, reasoning, planning, execution, and learning are distinct cognitive processes with clearly defined responsibilities.

